      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "aa958a34d98abcc629f2acddc63b003e0858fd8357a747b36ff9722bb8ec979b",
      "skos:note": "List of law enforcement officers and officials"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-telecommunications-interception-and-other-measures-act-2005#sch-1-sec-1",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "1 Section 473.1 of the Criminal Code (at the end of the",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 8,
      "values:originalText": "definition of law enforcement officer)\nAdd:\n\n(g) a member of the New South Wales Crime Commission or a\nmember of the staff of that Commission;\n\n(h) an officer of the Independent Commission Against\nCorruption of New South Wales, being a person who is an\nofficer as defined by the Independent Commission Against\nCorruption Act 1988 of New South Wales;\n\n(i) the Commissioner of the Police Integrity Commission of\nNew South Wales, an Assistant Commissioner of that\nCommission or a member of the staff of that Commission;\n\n(j) an officer of the Corruption and Crime Commission of\nWestern Australia within the meaning of the Corruption and\nCrime Commission Act 2003 of Western Australia;\n\n(k) an authorised commission officer of the Crime and\nMisconduct Commission of Queensland within the meaning\nof the Crime and Misconduct Act 2001 of Queensland.\n\nAmendment of the Telecommunications (Interception) Act 1979  Schedule 2\nEmergency services  Part 1\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Telecommunications Interception and Other Measures) Act 2005\nNo. 95, 2005            5"
    },
