    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-telecommunications-interception-and-other-measures-act-2005-sch-2-sec-1",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "1 Subsections 6(2A) and (2B)",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-telecommunications-interception-and-other-measures-act-2005#sch-2-sec-1"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-telecommunications-interception-and-other-measures-act-2005.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-telecommunications-interception-and-other-measures-act-2005.pdf, p.9",
      "values:originalText": "Repeal the subsections, substitute:\nCommunications to or from emergency service facilities\n\n(2A) In this section, emergency service facility means premises that are\ndeclared by the Minister, by written instrument, to be an\nemergency service facility.\n\n(2B) The Minister may declare premises to be an emergency service\nfacility if the Minister is satisfied that the premises are operated by:\n\n(a) a police force or service of the Commonwealth, of a State or\nof the Australian Capital Territory; or\n\n(b) a fire service of a State or of the Australian Capital Territory;\nor\n\n(c) an ambulance service of a State or of the Australian Capital\nTerritory; or\n\n(d) a service for despatching, or referring matters for the\nattention of, a force or service referred to in paragraph (a), (b)\nor (c);\nto enable that force or service, or another force or service, to deal\nwith a request for assistance in an emergency.\n\n(2C) A declaration by the Minister under subsection (2B) is not a\nlegislative instrument for the purposes of the Legislative\nInstruments Act 2003.\n\n(2D) If the Minister makes a declaration under subsection (2B), the\nMinister must, by legislative instrument, specify:\n\n(a) the name of the force or service operating the premises to\nwhich the declaration relates; and\n\n(b) the geographical region in which those premises are located.\n\nSchedule 2  Amendment of the Telecommunications (Interception) Act 1979",
      "skos:definition": "Repeal the subsections, substitute:\nCommunications to or from emergency service facilities\n\n(2A) In this section, emergency service facility means premises that are\ndeclared by the Minister, by written instrument, to be an\nemergency service facility.\n\n(2B) The Minister may declare premises to be an emergency service\nfacility if the Minister is satisfied that the premises are operated by:\n\n(a) a police force or service of the Commonwealth, of a State or\nof the Australian Capital Territory; or\n\n(b) a fire service of a State or of the Australian Capital Territory;\nor\n\n(c) an ambulance service of a State or of the Australian Capital\nTerritory; or\n\n(d) a service for despatching, or referring matters for the\nattention of, a force or service referred to in paragraph (a), (b)\nor (c);\nto enable that force or service, or another force or service, to deal\nwith a request for assistance in an emergency.\n\n(2C) A declaration by the Minister under subsection (2B) is not a\nlegislative instrument for the purposes of the Legislative\nInstruments Act 2003.\n\n(2D) If the Minister makes a declaration under subsection (2B), the\nMinister must, by legislative instrument, specify:\n\n(a) the name of the force or service operating the premises to\nwhich the declaration relates; and\n\n(b) the geographical region in which those premises are located.\n\nSchedule 2  Amendment of the Telecommunications (Interception) Act 1979",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-telecommunications-interception-and-other-measures-act-2005-sch-2-sec-1-ss-2a"
        },
