      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-telecommunications-interception-and-other-measures-act-2005.pdf, p.12",
      "values:originalText": "class 1 offence)\nInsert:\n\nor (e) an offence constituted by receiving or assisting a person who\nis, to the offender’s knowledge, guilty of an offence of a kind\nreferred to in paragraph (a), (b), (c), (ca) or (cb), in order to\nenable the person to escape punishment or to dispose of the\nproceeds of the offence;\n\nAmendment of the Telecommunications (Interception) Act 1979  Schedule 2\nCivil forfeiture proceedings and named person warrants  Part 4\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Telecommunications Interception and Other Measures) Act 2005\nNo. 95, 2005            9",
      "skos:definition": "class 1 offence)\nInsert:\n\nor (e) an offence constituted by receiving or assisting a person who\nis, to the offender’s knowledge, guilty of an offence of a kind\nreferred to in paragraph (a), (b), (c), (ca) or (cb), in order to\nenable the person to escape punishment or to dispose of the\nproceeds of the offence;\n\nAmendment of the Telecommunications (Interception) Act 1979  Schedule 2\nCivil forfeiture proceedings and named person warrants  Part 4\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Telecommunications Interception and Other Measures) Act 2005\nNo. 95, 2005            9",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-telecommunications-interception-and-other-measures-act-2005-sch-2-sec-8-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-telecommunications-interception-and-other-measures-act-2005-sch-2-sec-8-2-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "3b263f9ded48a3e2d3ab3f3f7687cd91b6bbbc933e33a6c7b26aeda0121b48d7",
      "skos:note": "Receiving or assisting a person guilty of an offence to escape punishment or dispose of proceeds."
    },
    {
